 "posture": "Equity breadth is weakening: the TraderMonty composite sits at 39.5/100 (Weakening zone), with only 21% of the 75-name universe above its 50-day average and 35% above the 200-day, and all four major indexes are trading below both moving averages. VIX at 24.6 is in the cautious band and easing, but the tape is a rolling correction: the S&P has fallen five straight sessions to 7,324 (-6.3% from its Oct 6 high) while the Nasdaq is 11.5% off its record. Rates are the binding constraint - the 10Y at 5.07% plus FOMC minutes showing 'almost all' officials favor further hikes keep AI multiples under pressure despite Nvidia's strong print. Recommended posture: stay selective at 40-60% equity exposure, favor cash-rich quality over momentum, and treat rallies as suspect until breadth repairs.",
 "sentiment": "Risk-off lean with a hawkish-rates overlay: safe-haven bids in long bonds and cash, energy and healthcare sold, while VIX eased modestly - money is rotating out of the AI complex rather than panicking. Anthropic's record IPO debut today injects a wild card into AI sentiment.",
